As you know, we’ve not yet been able to include the DHL Sable load plan in the
Lido WAB interface, because the DHL LDM does not include actual values for zero
fuel weight and takeoff fuel (which are required for the WAB Planning Status
‘04’). And, DHL does not send an LSH like Amazon does.

So, we asked LSY to provide further information on the Planning Status ‘05’,
and we’ve decided to switch to this Planning Status and use the LDMs for the
Sable data.

Attached is the WAB Data Mapping document with the differences between the
LDM/LSH and ‘04’/’05’ Planning Status field populations highlighted in yellow.
The emails containing the Sable LDMs should follow the rules below.

SABLE Data (Amazon)

    Receiving Email Account: LoadManifest@atsginc.com
    Sending Email Account:  amazon-sable@amazon-wb.com
    Subject line beginning with ‘LDM’

SABLE Data (DHL)

    Receiving Email Account: LoadManifest@atsginc.com
    Sending Email Account:  avibar@dhl.com
    Subject line beginning with ‘LDM’

I know this will be a significant change to your programming, but hopefully it
will be straightforward and not be too time consuming.  Please leave the
current Sable LSH processing in place until we’re ready to test the new
version.  And save the current version, as we may find ourselves returning to
it!
